  "query_preview": "(Thursday through Sunday)... \nHigh pressure aloft will remain across northern Mexico and \nadjacent southwest states through the weekend with high \ntemperatures warming to around 5 degrees above average for\nThursday and Friday, and possibly to 5 to 10 degrees above average\nfor the coast and valleys on Saturday with an increase in surface\ndewpoints into the mid to upper 60s for coastal areas on Saturday.\n\nTropical Storm Polo, off the southwest coast of Mexico, is\nforecast by the National Hurricane center to become a major\nhurricane over the new few days with a track eventually and \ngenerally toward the west northwest which might put the center a \nfew hundred miles south of the southern tip of Baja on late Friday\nafternoon. The track uncertainty is even greater beyond Friday. \nThere could eventually be at least some peripheral impacts to \nportions of southern California for late in the weekend into early\nnext week.",
